From 17d4d717ec41ee1483d18b4964484e8ba030a1dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vxrn <vxrn@tutamail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:04:53 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the window mapped until the surface is destroyed

Attaching a NULL buffer unmaps the surface while the xdg-toplevel still
exists.  Compositors that animate window closing (Hyprland's windowsOut)
take the window snapshot on unmap, so they snapshot an empty frame and
the close animation runs on nothing.

The surface is destroyed a few lines below, and its buffers are released
by the compositor at that point, so there is nothing to free early.
---
 wayland.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wayland.c b/wayland.c
index f15c168..c7b5220 100644
--- a/wayland.c
+++ b/wayland.c
@@ -2297,10 +2297,14 @@
 
     wayl_roundtrip(win->term->wl);
 
-        /* Main window */
+    /* Main window
+     *
+     * Don't attach a NULL buffer here. That unmaps the surface while the
+     * toplevel still exists, and compositors that animate window closing
+     * snapshot the window on unmap: they get an empty frame, so the
+     * animation plays on nothing. The surface is destroyed just below, and
+     * the compositor releases its buffers at that point. */
     win->unmapped = true;
-    wl_surface_attach(win->surface.surf, NULL, 0, 0);
-    wl_surface_commit(win->surface.surf);
     wayl_roundtrip(win->term->wl);
 
     tll_free(win->on_outputs);
-- 
2.52.0

